  "body": "Packages and options live on separate tabs, and it's easy to land on the wrong one. Searching for a package name on the Options tab (or the other way round) just shows \"No options found!\" with no hint that you're on the wrong page.\n\nWhen a search comes up empty on packages or options, this adds a line pointing at the other tab, carrying the same query and channel over. On the options page it reads:\n\n> Looking for a package? **Search packages for oversteer** instead.\n\nClicking it lands on the packages tab with the query already filled in. Only the two main tabs are touched; the flakes tab and the modular-services view keep their current empty state.\n\nCloses #1062.\n",
  "closed_at": "2026-06-05T21:35:36Z",
